* @title ORDVST alphabetizes the &DUMP post-mortem listing
* @match substring
* @expect >>>
* TANGO = 1
* UNIFORM = 2
* VICTOR = 3
* ZULU = 4
* <<<
* Setting &DUMP triggers a post-mortem dump of every natural variable at
* termination. Unlike the DUMP() builtin (which lists storage order), the
* termination dump runs ORDVST first, so the listing is alphabetical. The four
* variables below are assigned out of order yet appear sorted, and they sort
* after every built-in pattern name so the run is contiguous.
        &DUMP = 1
        ZULU = 4
        TANGO = 1
        VICTOR = 3
        UNIFORM = 2
END
